## Perf: make Settings / Back End tab load fast (defer Lakebase/Delta cascade)

Context: The Settings → "Back End" tab felt slow because its loading spinner
gated the (minimal) backend selector on `refreshGraphDbTabFromServer()`, which
always ran the full Graph DB pipeline the Back End panel does not even display:
Delta warehouse listing, the Lakebase project→branch→database→schema cascade,
the Lakebase health probe (endpoint resolution + JWT mint + synchronous
Postgres connect), and optionally the UC catalog `SHOW CATALOGS`. That is
6–10 remote round-trips, mostly sequential, on every page load.

Fix: the Back End sub-page load now fetches ONLY the triple-store backend value
(a single GET behind its spinner). The graph engine JSON config and the
Lakebase/Delta remote cascade are deferred — loaded lazily the first time the
Lakebase/Delta sections are opened, or just-in-time before a Lakebase Save.

### Changes

1. `src/front/static/config/js/settings.js`
   - Split `refreshGraphDbTabFromServer()` into three:
     - `loadTripleStoreBackend()` — single GET `/settings/triple-store-backend`
       (the only thing the Back End sub-page displays).
     - `loadGraphEngineConfig()` — GETs `/graph-engine` + `/graph-engine-config`
       plus local-only form mirroring (`applyLakebaseFormFromConfigTextarea`,
       `prefillLakebaseConnectionFromConfig`). Needed by a Lakebase Save and as a
       prerequisite for the heavy cascade.
     - `loadGraphDbHeavyFromServer()` — Delta warehouse select, Lakebase project
       cascade, Lakebase health probe, and (managed_synced only) UC catalogs;
       loads `loadGraphEngineConfig()` first if not already done.
   - Split `setGraphDbTabLoading()` into `setBackendTabLoading()` (Back End
     banner/content only) and `setGraphDbHeavyLoading()` (Lakebase + Delta
     banners/panels only), so the Back End spinner covers only its own GET.
   - Page load now runs only `loadTripleStoreBackend()` and reveals the Back End
     panel immediately; everything else is deferred.
   - `sidebarSectionChanged`: lazily runs `loadGraphDbHeavyFromServer()` the
     first time `lakebase`/`delta` is opened (tracked by `graphDbHeavyLoaded`);
     revisiting `lakebase` refreshes health only.
   - Save path hardened: a Lakebase save first ensures `loadGraphEngineConfig()`
     ran (so the merge cannot blank the saved config); the Delta warehouse id is
     taken from the saved `currentDeltaWarehouseId` (not the empty live dropdown)
     when the heavy load has not run, and the post-save warehouse re-list is
     skipped unless the dropdown is live. New flags: `graphEngineConfigLoaded`,
     `graphDbHeavyLoaded`.

### Modified files

- `src/front/static/config/js/settings.js`

Tests: front-end only change (no Python impact); `uv run pytest -q -m "not scenario"` unaffected.
